Z||000008||Smoooooth GT||08-16-2001||09:21 PM||||Look's really good..  But, they do need glassing in for a more stock look.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Steve<BR><P>------------------<BR>NOS Injected 2.8L<BR>Future add's.. 2" drop, 17" wheel's, finish the turbo T-3watercooled project, ViperYellow           <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooth_sig2_3.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||pontiacs4me||08-16-2001||10:51 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Nashco:<BR><B>Aren't the elements going to be a little hard on your sub?<P><BR>Bryce<BR>88 GT</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>not at all.  because the vents are cut in above the radiatior not in the front trunk space.  these are fully functional vents.  <P>They can be placed up to 1 more inch foward to be as effective.  someone mentioned moving them more foward on the hood.  If they were moved more foward the openings would be right on top of the radiatior, and they wouldnt function as well as they do now.  <BR>When the fan is on you can feel air blowing out of the vent holes.  And at high speeds I know air is blowing out of there like crazy.  The shape of the vent creates a low pressure zone on the backside of the vent hole.  The high pressure that builds up in that area under the hood rushes out the hole to fill the low pressure zone.  This is how the shape of the vent helps to vent out the hot air off the superchargers in the GTP's.  With the fieros fan motor blowing air through it, it makes the vent that much more functionable.  <BR>As for blending it into the hood.  Ill get on that tomorrow.  I have the day off, and it is supposed to be nice.  Ill keep yall posted.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Nashco||08-17-2001||01:05 AM||||Doh..I'm such a dork.  I see what you mean pontiacs...I knew that, just didn't look closely enough.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
